--------------------------------------------------------------------
1. GRANT
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Subject to full payment of the agreed purchase price and execution of the
Source Code Bill of Sale (legal/SOURCE-CODE-BILL-OF-SALE.md) or an IP
Assignment (legal/IP-ASSIGNMENT-TEMPLATE.md), Licensor grants the named
buyer ("Buyer") ONE of the following estates, as specified in the signed
sale documents:

  (a) LICENSE MODEL — a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
      non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to use, modify, and
      internally deploy the Software for Buyer's own business, subject to
      the restrictions in Section 2; OR

  (b) ASSIGNMENT MODEL — full assignment of Licensor's copyright and
      associated intellectual-property rights in the Software to Buyer,
      subject to Section 4 (third-party components).

No other estate is granted. If no sale document has been executed, the
recipient has NO rights whatsoever and must delete the Software.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
2. RESTRICTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Unless the signed sale documents expressly state otherwise, Buyer may NOT:

  a. redistribute, resell, lease, lend, publish, or sublicense the Software
     (in whole or in part, modified or unmodified) to any third party;
  b. offer the Software, or any service whose essential value derives from
     the Software, to third parties as a product, template, or codebase;
  c. remove, alter, or obscure any proprietary notices, license texts, or
     attribution contained in the Software;
  d. use the Software to build a competing product for sale or distribution;
  e. represent that the Software's past performance guarantees future
     results. The Software executes trades with real funds; all trading
     outcomes are uncertain and Buyer assumes all financial risk.

